{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Not a dog shall sharpen its tongue.</b> I say that it is an expression of sharpening — he shall not sharpen it. And so ״לֹא חָרַץ לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל לְאִישׁ אֶת לְשׁוֹנוֹ״ (Joshua 10) — did not sharpen; ״אָז תֶּחֱרַץ״ (II Samuel 5:24) — you shall sharpen; ״לְמוֹרַג חָרוּץ״ (Isaiah 41) — sharpened; ״מַחְשְׁבוֹת חָרוּץ״ (Proverbs 21) — a sharp and sharpened man; ״וְיַד חֲרוּצִים תַּעֲשִׁיר״ (ibid. 10) — sharp ones, sharpened merchants." "<b>That shall be distinguished.</b> He will distinguish."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:28.740344625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}